.TH SLACK-AXI 1 "August 19, 2026" "slack-axi-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slack-axi - agent-facing Slack CLI with bounded reads and signed staged writes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slack-axi
[global options] command [command options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every stdout path is one slack-axi/v1 envelope encoded as strict TOON by default, or JSON/JSONL when requested. Operational failures exit 1 and invalid usage exits 2. Diagnostics appear on stderr only with --verbose.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
--workspace selects a configured alias or team ID. --output defaults to toon. --fields validates command-specific field names. --limit bounds collections. --cursor continues stable pages. --full expands long text. --verbose enables redacted diagnostics.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS AUTH
Manage Slack workspace authentication.
.PP
Defaults: Global --output toon; no command-specific defaults.
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi auth list
.fi
.nf
slack-axi auth doctor --workspace work
.fi
.SS AUTH ADD
Import one bounded browser-session or user-token JSON object from stdin into macOS Keychain.
.PP
Defaults: browser mode with exact xoxc and xoxd fields; stdin is capped at 16,384 UTF-8 bytes
.br
Incompatible combinations: --browser is an explicit synonym for the default and conflicts with --user-token; credentials are accepted only through --from-stdin and never through argv.
.nf
slack-axi auth add work --from-stdin < /secure/path/browser-session.json
.fi
.nf
slack-axi auth add work --user-token --from-stdin < /secure/path/user-token.json
.fi
.SS AUTH LIST
List configured workspaces without reading credentials.
.PP
Defaults: Global --output toon; no command-specific defaults.
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi auth list
.fi
.nf
slack-axi auth list --output json
.fi
.SS AUTH USE
Select the default workspace.
.PP
Defaults: Global --output toon; no command-specific defaults.
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi auth use work
.fi
.nf
slack-axi auth use T012ABC
.fi
.SS AUTH REVOKE
Stage revocation of one imported xoxp user token.
.PP
Defaults: staged only; browser sessions must be terminated in Slack before local removal; does not uninstall the Slack app or remove local data
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi auth revoke work
.fi
.nf
slack-axi auth revoke T012ABC --workspace T012ABC
.fi
.SS AUTH REMOVE
Remove a local workspace, its Keychain credentials, caches, and action records.
.PP
Defaults: does not terminate a browser session, revoke a user token, or uninstall an app at Slack; failed local cleanup remains pending for auth doctor
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi auth remove work
.fi
.nf
slack-axi auth remove T012ABC
.fi
.SS AUTH DOCTOR
Independently probe and persist public and browser-private Slack capabilities.
.PP
Defaults: Global --output toon; no command-specific defaults.
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi auth doctor
.fi
.nf
slack-axi auth doctor --workspace work
.fi
.SS SYNC
Refresh bounded workspace entity and inbox caches.
.PP
Defaults: two pages per paged source
.br
Incompatible combinations: --all requires --max-pages <1..100>; --max-pages is invalid without --all.
.nf
slack-axi sync --workspace work
.fi
.nf
slack-axi sync --all --max-pages 20 --workspace work
.fi
.SS CONVERSATION
Discover and inspect channels and DMs.
.PP
Defaults: Global --output toon; no command-specific defaults.
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi conversation list
.fi
.nf
slack-axi conversation get '#eng'
.fi
.SS CONVERSATION LIST
List cached conversations with authoritative coverage.
.PP
Defaults: --limit 20; archived conversations excluded
.br
Incompatible combinations: None.
.nf
slack-axi conversation list
.fi
.nf
